Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: remove implicit latest-WireGuard network fetch

The vendor Kbuild.include invokes a downloader on each recursive make. This
port disables that old out-of-tree kernel driver and Tailscale uses its own
userspace WireGuard implementation over TUN. Keep the kernel source pinned
and avoid both unrequested network downloads and repeated build-time lookups.

--- a/scripts/Kbuild.include
+++ b/scripts/Kbuild.include
@@ -276,4 +276,3 @@
 
 echo-why = $(call escsq, $(strip $(why)))
 endif
-$(shell cd "$(srctree)" && ./scripts/fetch-latest-wireguard.sh)
